    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d239-a10">

                <pb facs="0350" n="244" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg244"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 9 in No 237].</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. McCreery to Mr. Egan</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Valparaiso</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-11-20"><hi rendition="#italic">November 20,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In the case of Patrick Shields, of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Keweenaw</hi>, who makes a claim against the Government
                    of Chile for injuries claimed to have been received at the hands of the police
                    of this city, I desire to state that the crew list of the steamship shows that
                    he was born in Ireland and is a subject of Great Britain.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wm. B. McCreery</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">United States Consul</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
